{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1520282-creating-spirits-spirits-classifications","id":1520282,"title":"Creating spirits & spirits classifications","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-08-10T03:59:30-07:00","id":1520282,"title":"Creating spirits & spirits classifications","content":"Hey there,<br /> <br /> So I always felt that the basic description of C\u00e9leste &gt; Incarna &gt; Jagglins &gt; Gafflins was a bit simplistic and I nuanced it a lot (like with minor and major in each category at least). Now I was wondering do we have anywhere some indicators of how much stats/charms a spirit should have depending of his rank ? Because some spirits, like minor elementals can sometime feel quite powerful. \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8944-tanakyelle","name":"Tanakyelle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8944_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T11:54:45-07:00","id":1520315,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, not really. Spirits are one of the few entities that never got a playable splat, aside from Possessed, and so the rules for creating them vary between game lines and purpose. There are rules for making personal Totems (mostly Jagglings) but the result is often on par with Gaffling examples from elsewhere. With the exception of the Familiar/Numen of one of my player's characters, I have never made a Spirit from scratch and instead reskinned an example Spirit that was closest to what I needed.<br /> <br /> For W20 the rule of thumb is Willpower + Rage + Gnosis = Essence, with Gafflings around 20 Essence and one or two extra Charms, Jagglings around 30 Essence with three or more extra Charms.<br /> Revised era Spirits follow the same rule (but with Power = Essence x2) and tend to be a lot beefier in both stats and Charms.<br /> <br /> Either way, since Essence is the sum of stats, it's a good power gauge and probably should inform the number of extra charms as well. So, maybe one extra charm for every 10 points of Essence.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-10T12:08:23-07:00","id":1520318,"title":"","content":"I think the distinctions were just a very general power level / function that was purposefully meant to vague and unspecific. That's a strength and not a weakness to me. Obviously the Celestines and Incarna are so powerful that it is meaningless to give them statistics. It only at the level of Jagglings and Gafflings that we need to concentrate on.<br /> <br /> Most spirits described in the sourcebooks are meant to be Gafflings. They are generic spirits of that type. They are meant to be the servants and minions of more powerful spirits. They also lack free will and just follow their basic &quot;programming&quot; in terms of how they act. While they can communicate to others, they really cannot be reasoned with. PCs attempting to communicate with them are in the same way as humans communicating with wild animals. You may be able to befriend them, gain their trust, make them afraid of you, etc., but you cannot actually reason with them because they are almost mindless. They will always react in a way aligned with their instinct/purpose/nature.<br /> <br /> Jagglings are either those spirits with individual names or have specific functions. They are the ones who have free will, individual personalities, and can make their own schemes. They are actually &quot;people&quot; in a roleplaying sense. If an ST wants PCs to have real roleplaying encounters with spirits, establish real relationships, be wrapped up in plots, these are the spirits to use. <br /> <br /> Using Stag's Brood in Axis Mundi as an example, most of the spirits are examples of Gafflings. But I would classify Dawn, Hind, and Yale as distinct Jagglings because they appear to be distinct individual spirits as opposed to a broad type. There are likely no Gafflings of these spirits at all. And perhaps only one such Jaggling in existence (though if anything happens to them, then Stag or some other Incarna could/will create a replacement.) I also believe that spirits like Grain, Impala, the Brook, Rabbit, and Squirrel - as statted - are also supposed to be Jagglings, probably a jaggling avatar of a lesser Incarna. The description of Squirrel specifically says it is a jaggling avatar. These spirits would also have less powerful Gaffling spirits of that same type with lower stats and fewer charms. And there can be multiple jaggling avatars of these lesser Incarna in existence at the same time. The world is very big after all.<br /> <br /> I don't think it is a scenario where all Jagglings are more powerful than all Gafflings. I think it is OK for elemental spirits to be more powerful than say animal spirits (both gafflings and jaggling). Animals by their very nature are less powerful and more finite than more fundamental and primal forces. No elephant is going to be able to beat a volcano if it erupts. Certain Gafflings could even be more powerful than individual Jagglings depending on what each represents. So I would be against any idea of limiting stats based on Jaggling/Gaffling rank (for example, no Gafflings can have more than 5 in any trait).<br /> <br /> What you want to do is make Jagglings of a certain spirit type more powerful than its Gafflings of the <i>same</i> spirit type. And that is done just by boosting some of its stats a bit, increasing Essence, and giving them some additional (and appropriate) Charms. And of course giving them actual personalities and free will.<br /> <br /> I would keep Gafflings as generic as possible, and not change their stats. I might make some more experienced Gafflings have higher Essence, but that's all. I would be open that some Gafflings who have had enough encounters, chiminage, relationship with non-spirits, etc. make the transition to Jaggling status and somehow gaining true sapience. Either because that is natural to happen at some point, or because the Incarna elevates that spirit. If that happens, then it can begin developing better stats and Charms as a Jaggling.<br /> <br /> What distinguishes Jagglings and Gafflings is not their power level, but that they have free will and thus individual personalities and goals/purposes. (And possibly that they can command those lesser Gafflings that they created to serve them). And also that because they have special place in the hierarchy of the Major Incarna or spirit brood, that other spirits treat them appropriately as benefits their rank and position. If there is only one Hind or one Yale at any time, than even very powerful deer jagglings with just as much power as them will likely defer to them because they serve a very special purpose for Stag.<br /> <br /> Jagglings created to be caern totems are going to be different than Jagglings acting as pack totems which will also be different from Jagglings that are just meant to guide/protect other spirits of their kind. Squirrel jagglings in each of those roles will be very different even though all are still &quot;Squirrel jaggling&quot; and even if they all have the exact same stats. They'll be acting very differently because they have different personalities and duties (protecting the caern, guiding a pack, overseeing that squirrels are fulfilling their purpose in Gaia's plan).<br /> <br /> Of course, Jagglings can vary in power considerably. But I would always keep it in the context of what that spirit represents and its purpose. So maybe there is some kind of deer spirit more powerful than the elemental Gafflings, but I wouldn't make it more powerful than most elemental Jagglings (like Gortak or Salamander in Axis Mundi) who would have very specific purposes as to the fundamental needs of Gaia as planet.<br /> <br /> As an ST, you want to use either Gafflings or Jagglings based on your narrative needs. If you just need a spirit to be there to do generic stuff, then keep them Gafflings. If you actually want roleplaying elements, than make that spirit a Jaggling instead.<br /> <br /> This is how I try to handle it at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}